Phishing Awareness Guide 

Introduction 
Click zero is a cybersecurity awareness guide developed to educate users about phishing attacks and promote safe online activities. The guide helps users identify suspicious emails and messages to avoid being victims of phishing attacks.
What is phishing?
It is a cybercrime attack where criminals send fraudulent messages and emails that trick people into revealing their sensitive details such as financial information and passwords.
Common phishing techniques
•	Spear phishing- cybercriminals target specific individuals through personalised messages
•	Smishing- criminals send fraudulent emails and messages to trick people into clicking malicious links.
•	Email phishing- attackers pretend to be trusted organisations such as banks and send fake emails.
Warning signs of phishing 
•	Urgent or threatening messages 
•	Request for login credentials such as passwords 
•	Unusual sender addresses
•	Suspicious links or website addresses
Prevention of phishing attacks
•	Users should avoid clicking unknown and suspicious emails and opening attachments.\
•	Verify sender addresses and confirm with sources before responding.
•	Report emails and messages which look suspicious.
Important Security Warning
STOP! THINK! VERIFY!
Never trust unexpected notification messages that request for login credentials, financial information or any confidential. Always verify links and attachments before clicking and downloading.
Reporting phishing attacks 
Report to organisations IT department or cybersecurity help desk when receiving a suspicious message 
Conclusion 
Phishing attacks can lead to exposure of personal and sensitive organisational information. Knowing and understanding warning signs helps  reduce the risk of phishing attacks. It is everyone’s responsibility to understand cyber threats and practice safe online activities to reduce the risk of cyberattacks and secure their digital information.
